  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'ve carefully reviewed the user requirements. I\'ve pinpointed the key aspects: \"Gk Services\" as the car service center name, and the critical responsive sizing for desktop, tablet, and mobile, with the breakpoints defined at 1200px, 1024px, and 767px respectively. Additionally, I\'ve noted the need for global font specifications, including primary and secondary fonts.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Style**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the aesthetic direction. I\'ve chosen a professional, futuristic, and cyberpunk-inspired color scheme: Deep Void Obsidian with Neon Cyan/Electric Blue, complemented by Precision Titanium Grey. I\'m visualizing the static page with six sections, starting with a Hero section showcasing a futuristic hyper-car and a tagline. Next, I\'m designing a 360\302\260 interactive car inspection with before/after service hotspots.\n\n\n**Outlining Site Structure**\n\nI\'m solidifying the website\'s structure now. Section 3 will focus on Quantum Diagnostics and Core Services. Section 4 will highlight the Live Robotic Bay and Tech Stack. Section 5 will concentrate on the Client Experience, including an interactive service calculator and booking terminal. Finally, Section 6 will present Futuristic Testimonials and details on the GK Fleet Network, alongside an FAQ or guarantee.\n\n\n**Refining UI Interactions**\n\nI\'m now detailing user interface behaviors. I\'m focusing on a \"lift\" hover effect translating elements on the y-axis, coupled with futuristic glows and border illumination. Each section\'s design will be unique to maintain user engagement. The footer will be comprehensive, including all necessary professional details and telemetry. I\'ve also planned a responsive hamburger menu for tablet and mobile devices. Finally, I\'m thinking about the code export, potentially using JSZip for a downloadable ZIP archive.\n\n\n"
