  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n*   **Create Footer Component:** (Requirement 7) Needs to be professional and contain necessary details.\n    *   Status: NOT STARTED\n*   **Assemble `App.tsx`:** Integrate all 6 sections (Hero, 360 Viewer, Services, Tech Bays, Cost Calculator, Footer) into the main application file, ensuring smooth scrolling and state management for modals.\n    *   Status: NOT STARTED\n*   **Generate ZIP File:** (Requirement 11) Package the final code for the user.\n    *   Status: NOT STARTED\n*   **Final Review:** Verify all requirements (responsive design, hover effects, 360 rotation, hamburger menu, futuristic theme).\n    *   Status: NOT STARTED\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n\n*   **Theme:** \"Futuristic professional static webpage\" for \"Gk Services\" (Car service center).\n*   **Design Preferences:**\n    *   \"Responsive size for the devices [desktop over 1200px, tab over 1024, mobile over 767]\".\n    *   \"Global color palette use professional palette for 2 color that are compatible with each other\".\n    *   \"Header [sticky ! important] that has 3 division An logo Gk and the navigation menu and the contact button which has hovering effects that the button effect should applied universally fro all the button in the page\".\n    *   \"All the element should hae an hover effect of yaxis -30 as whole container\".\n    *   \"Navigation menu should turn to hamburger menu in the tab and the mobile view\".\n    *   \"Site needs to be highly futuristic\".\n*   **Functionality:**\n    *   \"Add section where the user can view that their car[the car is 360 rotatable- before after service enhancement in the most playfull way like they can scroll the car and look when they click an certain part it open an popup showing before and after popup showing the details that are before and after.\"\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n\n*   **Project Setup:** Initialized project structure and metadata.\n*   **Design System:** Configured `src/index.css` with futuristic typography (`Orbitron`, `Rajdhani`, `Inter`, `JetBrains Mono`), color variables, and responsive font sizing rules. Implemented universal button hover effects and the `gk-hover-lift` class for the required y-axis -30px container lift.\n*   **Data Layer:** Created `src/types.ts` for type definitions and `src/data/mockCarData.ts` containing the 360-degree car angles, hotspots, service pillars, tech chambers, testimonials, and FAQ data.\n*   **Component Development:**\n    *   `Header.tsx`: Implemented sticky header with 3 divisions, responsive hamburger menu, and universal button styles.\n    *   `BeforeAfterModal.tsx`: Created the interactive comparison modal with a slider and telemetry data display.\n    *   `Car360Viewer.tsx`: Implemented the interactive 360-degree viewer with scroll/drag rotation, hotspot pins, and HUD overlays.\n    *   `HeroSection.tsx`: Created the hero section with futuristic branding and CTA buttons.\n    *   `ServicesSection.tsx`: Created the core services matrix.\n    *   `TechBaySection.tsx`: Created the robotic bay telemetry display.\n    *   `CostCalculatorSection.tsx`: Created the service estimator terminal.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n\n*   **Design System:** The futuristic aesthetic relies on the `gk-hover-lift` class (transitioning `transform: translateY(-30px)` and adding a glow shadow) and the `gk-btn` class (which uses a custom `clip-path` and a sweeping neon hover effect).\n*   **360 Viewer:** The viewer uses an array of image objects (`CAR_360_ANGLES`) and updates the `currentAngleIndex` based on mouse/touch drag or scroll wheel events. Hotspots are mapped using percentage-based positioning (`xPercent`, `yPercent`) and are filtered based on the `visibleAngles` array.\n*   **State Management:** The `BeforeAfterModal` is controlled by a parent component passing a `hotspot` object. The `Car360Viewer` manages its own rotation state.\n*   **Constraints:** Image generation failed due to usage limits; placeholders or existing Unsplash URLs are used.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n\n*   **Edited/Created Files:**\n    *   `/metadata.json`: Updated with title and description.\n    *   `/index.html`: Added Google Fonts (`Inter`, `JetBrains Mono`, `Orbitron`, `Rajdhani`) and meta tags.\n    *   `/src/index.css`: Added design system, responsive rules, and hover effects.\n    *   `/src/types.ts`: Created interface definitions.\n    *   `/src/data/mockCarData.ts`: Created mock data.\n    *   `/src/components/Header.tsx`: Created header component.\n    *   `/src/components/BeforeAfterModal.tsx`: Created modal component.\n    *   `/src/components/Car360Viewer.tsx`: Created 360 viewer component.\n    *   `/src/components/HeroSection.tsx`: Created hero section.\n    *   `/src/components/ServicesSection.tsx`: Created services section.\n    *   `/src/components/TechBaySection.tsx`: Created tech bay section.\n    *   `/src/components/CostCalculatorSection.tsx`: Created calculator section.\n\n*   **Viewed Files:**\n    *   `/src/index.css`: Key for design system implementation.\n    *   `/src/data/mockCarData.ts`: Key for understanding the data structure used by components.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n*   **Immediate Next Step:** Create `src/components/Footer.tsx`.\n*   **Following Step:** Assemble all components into `src/App.tsx`.\n*   **Final Step:** Generate the ZIP file for the user.\n*   **Context:** The project is in the IMPLEMENTATION phase. The core components are built; they now need to be integrated into the main application structure and finalized with a footer."
    included_step_index_end: 40
    conversation_log_uris: "file:///.aistudio/artifacts/brain/58bed46a-6c55-40a4-8ff1-56b4e10af129/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl"
    user_requests: "User prompt: need to buid an futuristic professional static webpage- conditions and\nrequirements\n\n1.  regarding an Car service center - \"Gk Services\" 2.use responsive size for\n    the devices [desktop over 1200px,tab over 1024, mobile over 767 -]for the\n    Global font -\n\n  - primary ,secondary-[your wish ]\n  - text ,accent -prompt\n\n3.  global color palette use professional palette for 2 color that are\n    compatible with each other\n4.  the static page should contain 6 section\n5.  the page should have an header [sticky ! important ] that has 3 division An\n    logo Gk and the navigation menu and the contact button which has hovering\n    effects that the button effect should applied universally fro all the button\n    in the page 6.the section should be attaractive and engaging each should be\n    different from the other 7.the footer should be professional with the\n    necessary details\n6.  all the element should hae an hover effect of yaxis -30 as whole container\n7.  the navigation menu should turn to hamburger menuin the tab andt he\n    mobileview 10.generate the media that is required generate it according to\n    the site 11.generate the code and get the zip file for the the further\n    instruction it shuold be easily editable\n8.  the site needs to be highly futuristic 13.add section where the user can\n    view that their car[the car is 360 rotatable- before after service\n    enhancement in the most playfull way like they can scroll the car and look\n    when they click an certain part it open an popup showing before and after\n    popup showing the details that are before and after.\n\ngenerate zip and an preview of the code\n\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
