  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering User Interface Changes**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a better handle on the user\'s requests. I\'m focusing on implementing the \"light/dark\" button with entirely opposing color palettes. This includes making the \"back to top\" button with scroll percentage functionality and adjusting the car rotation to a single-car view, not all. I\'ll need to figure out how to best integrate these elements into a user-friendly interface.\n\n\n**Implementing Font and Mode**\n\nRight now, I\'m swapping out the font. I\'ve imported both Chakra Petch and Michroma, and I\'m playing with a primary font setting. It looks sharp. Also, I\'m setting up dark mode by initializing `<html class=\"dark\">` and defining contrasting color palettes for both light and dark. I\'m focusing on clean, angular visuals. I think I will prioritize the \"light/dark\" button and back-to-top button next.\n\n\n**Refining Theme Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m zeroing in on the light theme\'s design. I\'ve chosen Deep Slate Obsidian text with High-Voltage Electric Cyan and Velocity Blue accents. I am also implementing a Cyber-grid in light mode. This includes crisp white and slate backgrounds with vibrant cyan/blue borders for buttons. I\'m focusing on creating that pristine, high-tech Formula 1 dock feel, contrasting directly with the dark mode.\n\n\n**Designing Scroll-Driven Visuals**\n\nI\'m now implementing the scroll-percentage circle. It will dynamically fill with electric cyan, displaying the numerical percentage and an upward arrow on hover. Clicking it will scroll smoothly to the top. I aim for it to be accessible, sleek, and responsive, with a circumference proportional to the radius. I am looking forward to seeing it working!\n\n**Developing Car Rotation**\n\nI\'m now creating a 3D inspection studio for a single hypercar, removing the previous multiple-car view. The user will have a 360\302\260 view including over, under, and sideways angles. I am designing several distinct elevation angles. \"OVER_CAR\" will provide a top-down view, while \"EYE_LEVEL\" provides a sideways 360\302\260 orbital ring.\n\n\n**Constructing Interactive Undercarriage**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in building the interactive undercarriage view, focusing on detailed hotspots. I\'m excited about the transparent, isolated car render. This includes a holographic turntable with LiDAR lines and ground shadows, plus hotspots for the Venturi tunnel, high-flow exhaust, magnetic dampers, and carbon skid plate.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 186023959
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
