  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining View Types**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the different view types for the `Car360Viewer.tsx` component. The key here is flexibility; I\'ve decided to support three distinct perspectives: an eye-level orbit view, a top-down aerial view, and an undercarriage view. I\'m prioritizing clarity in these distinctions for the initial implementation.\n\n\n**Establishing State Management**\n\nNow, I\'m concentrating on the state variables needed for the car viewer. I\'m setting up variables for elevation (orbit, over, under), rotation index, pitch, auto-rotation flag, dragging status, zoom levels, and wireframe mode.\n\nI\'m focused on the visual presentation and have decided on a holographic turntable with a transparent background. I\'m adding a circular degree ruler, an animated radar sweep, and real-time 3D coordinate telemetry. Interactive view switcher tabs will allow elevation adjustments.\n\n\n**Refining View Transitions**\n\nI\'m now refining the animations between views. The \'top-down\' transition shows the car\'s carbon roof and wing. I\'m especially focused on the \'under\' view, smoothly transitioning to the chassis to highlight venturi tunnels and suspension. I want the \'orbit\' to rotate smoothly at eye-level.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
