  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding Fonts for Enhancement**\n\nI\'m currently working on incorporating `Space Grotesk`, `Plus Jakarta Sans`, and `Orbitron` into the project via Google Fonts, and the initial integration is going well. I\'m adding these fonts directly into the HTML to streamline loading, using a standard link tag. I am excited to see how these fonts change the appearance of the project!\n\n\n**Defining Font and Color Schemes**\n\nI\'ve just defined the light mode color scheme in `src/index.css` by assigning the chosen fonts (`Space Grotesk`, `Plus Jakarta Sans`, and `JetBrains Mono`) to specific CSS variables, along with the color palette. This includes primary, secondary, and body font assignments, alongside background, text, and border colors. Next, I\'ll be implementing the dark mode color scheme.\n\n\n**Implementing Dark Mode**\n\nI\'ve just finished the dark mode CSS variables within `src/index.css`, establishing a new color scheme and font assignments: `Chakra Petch`, `Michroma`, `Rajdhani`, `Inter`, and `JetBrains Mono`. I\'m using a \'Cyber Titanium Void\' theme and have defined the corresponding background, text, and border colors for a complete dark mode experience. I\'m excited with the user comment that dark mode is now okay!\n\n\n**Refining Responsive Text**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring the text is responsive across all devices. I\'ve examined `src/index.css` and all related components to implement responsive font rules. I\'m using `clamp()` to dynamically adjust font sizes for various screen sizes, specifically for mobile devices. I\'m aiming for optimal readability across different viewports.\n\n\n**Scaling Text Across Devices**\n\nI\'ve just added detailed responsive font size adjustments within `src/index.css`! I\'ve created media queries for mobile, tablet, and desktop viewports, using `clamp()` to set dynamic font sizes for `display`, `h2`, `h3`, `body`, and `sub` elements. I also included `white-space: nowrap` for buttons and other UI elements to manage content overflow.\n\n\n**Adjusting for Mobile Responsiveness**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the layout and content display for various screen sizes, especially mobile devices. I\'m carefully reviewing and adjusting the padding, text sizes, and component visibility based on the viewport to ensure that there\'s no text clipping or overlap. I\'m paying close attention to the specific requirements for mobile views, ensuring only the company logo and hamburger menu are visible in the header. The navigation menu links are being implemented in the offcanvas content drawer, as required.\n\n\n**Designing the Offcanvas Drawer**\n\nI\'m currently designing an offcanvas sidebar to enhance the user experience on tablets and mobile devices. When the hamburger button is tapped, a drawer smoothly slides in from the right, complete with a backdrop overlay. The drawer will include the company badge, all navigation links, action buttons, location details, operating hours, and an emergency hotline. Tapping any link or the backdrop closes the drawer.\n\n**Updating Light/Dark Button Position**\n\nI\'m repositioning the light/dark mode button above the \"back to top\" button. I\'ve considered creating a floating control cluster in `src/components/BackToTopWithScrollPercentage.tsx`, or passing the theme and toggle function to this component. I plan to style the light/dark mode button as a sleek circular button, positioned at the bottom-right corner.\n\n\n**Constructing 3D Model**\n\nI\'m now diving into building the interactive 3D car model using Three.js within `src/components/Car3DCanvas.tsx`. I\'m using `THREE.Scene`, `THREE.PerspectiveCamera`, `THREE.WebGLRenderer`, and various light sources. I\'m focusing on crafting a procedural, aerodynamic supercar with a metallic paint material for the main body. I\'m starting with an `ExtrudeGeometry` or multi-segment `BoxGeometry` and `CylinderGeometry` for the tapered chassis.\n\n\n**Detailing 3D Car Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the aerodynamic details and lights of the 3D car model! I\'m adding sculpted carbon fiber side pods and splitters, plus a curved cockpit canopy with tinted glass. I\'m excited to integrate a rear active aero wing with carbon fiber pylons and angled main planes. I\'ll add high-intensity LED headlights, quad laser taillights, and glowing exhaust tips, too. Plus, four high-detail wheels!\n\n\n**Adding Brake & Studio Effects**\n\nI\'m now integrating neon glowing Brembo-style brake calipers into the model at the 10 and 2 o\'clock positions. I\'m also adding a reflective dark/light studio turntable floor with subtle grid lines and an outer glowing circular laser ring that matches the 360-degree turntable. Plus, there\'s an ambient contact shadow disk under the car.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Interactive Hotspots**\n\nI\'m now implementing interactive hotspots on the 3D model, with pulsed badges floating above specific car components. I\'ve projected each hotspot\'s 3D coordinate to 2D screen coordinates, ready to display telemetry cards on hover and open before-and-after comparison modals on click. I am adding labels for autonomous diagnostic scans, cryogenic blasts, and other components, along with a LiDAR wireframe scan mode. The LiDAR mode renders the entire model as a neon glowing cyber wireframe. I can\'t wait!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 834224834
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
