    thinking: "**Examining Overlap Behavior**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the off-canvas hamburger menu\'s overlap issue. I\'ve pinpointed `Header.tsx` and am analyzing the relevant JSX code. Specifically, the `div` with `id=\"offcanvas-navigation-overlay\"` seems crucial, particularly the `z-50` and positioning classes. I\'m exploring how these attributes interact to ensure correct overlaying behavior.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Overlay Fix**\n\nOkay, the overlay problem stemmed from nesting the off-canvas within the sticky header\'s stacking context. The `header`\'s `z-50`, height, and potential transforms caused clipping. Using a React Portal (`createPortal`) to render the overlay directly on `document.body` resolved this. Ensuring full viewport height for the sliding drawer and a high z-index is the next task. I plan on incorporating smooth slide-in animations as well.\n\n\n**Deciphering Model URL**\n\nI\'ve just been looking at that Sketchfab link you provided. My focus is understanding the structure, extracting the model ID, and figuring out how to embed the model. I\'ve successfully extracted the model ID and found its direct embed format. I\'m now testing the official Sketchfab 3D WebGL viewer embed iframe URL for its validity and compatibility.\n\n\n**Validating Viewer Options**\n\nI\'ve confirmed full 3D interaction is enabled in the Sketchfab embed; it\'s a powerful WebGL viewer! I can now envision embedding this model directly in `Car360Viewer.tsx`, complete with custom HUD controls. Moreover, I\'m defining the available modes: a dedicated \"Sketchfab 3D Sports Car\" mode using the provided model, a procedural Three.js model, and a multi-elevation studio view. This looks promising.\n\n\n**Refining Navigation Clarity**\n\nI\'m focused on decluttering the navigation menu. The current titles are lengthy and cause congestion, especially on smaller screens. I\'m streamlining these to be more concise: \"Overview,\" \"3D Inspection,\" \"Services,\" \"Technology,\" \"Estimator,\" and \"Reviews.\" This will improve readability and spacing, resulting in a cleaner user experience. I\'m also planning to explore hiding buttons in the mobile header for further simplification.\n\n\n"
