  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Inspecting the Link Details**\n\nOkay, I\'m now delving into the provided link. It seems to point towards a 3D model of a sports car, hosted on Sketchfab. The specific query used to find the image was \"3d model of sports car.\" I\'m examining the image URL and associated data to understand its context and attributes better, to determine how relevant it is for the user.\n\n\n**Constructing the 3D Component**\n\nI\'ve extracted the core data from the link and have a solid plan. I am building a dedicated `SketchfabCarModel.tsx` component, allowing the car model to be rendered interactively. The `Car360Viewer.tsx` component will now offer the user the option to view the specific sports car (identified by the model ID `dba4f043e0974054b5756d601ff5c256`) as an interactive 3D model.\n\n\n**Developing Advanced Visuals**\n\nI\'m now integrating advanced 3D features. I plan to use the car model with interactive paint finishes, LiDAR wireframe mode, and live 3D coordinate hotspots! I am exploring ways to embed the Sketchfab iframe seamlessly, and considering fallback handling and quick reload options for reliability. Full interactive controls and a direct link badge to the Sketchfab model will be included.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Z-Index Issues**\n\nI\'m digging into why the off-canvas menu might be overlapping. I\'ve pinpointed the issue in `Header.tsx`. It seems that the overlay\'s z-index needs adjustment due to how the header handles fixed positioning and CSS effects such as `backdrop-blur-sm`. I\'m examining how the parent header\'s styling influences the positioning of its child, the off-canvas menu, to ensure they don\'t overlap.\n\n\n**Fixing the Overlay Behavior**\n\nI\'ve fixed the z-index issue. The off-canvas menu was being trapped or clipped within the 80px header. Using `createPortal` with `document.body` ensures it now overlaps the entire viewport, including the sticky header, with `position: fixed` and `z-index: 99999`. This guarantees the overlay\'s darkness and correct sliding behavior. I\'ve now verified that `document.body` is indeed accessible and am implementing the menu rewrite and mobile button hiding for Requirement 3.\n\n\n**Refining the Menu Content**\n\nI\'ve streamlined the desktop menu headings to reduce congestion. I\'ve replaced \"Mission Hub\" with \"Overview,\" \"360\302\260 Car Scan\" with \"3D Inspection,\" \"Services Matrix\" with \"Services,\" \"Robotic Bays\" with \"Technology,\" \"Cost Terminal\" with \"Estimator,\" and \"Reviews & FAQ\" with \"Reviews.\" The rewritten headings enhance readability with comfortable spacing and refined font styling.\n\n\n**Adjusting the Mobile Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the mobile header. I\'ve streamlined the headings and I\'m currently refining the mobile view. The goal is to ensure a clean, uncluttered layout. I am reviewing the logic within the `Header.tsx` to hide unnecessary elements on smaller screens, specifically the buttons, leaving only the hamburger menu visible. I am also making sure that the buttons from the drawer are spacious.\n\n\n**Configuring the Mobile Header**\n\nI\'m now implementing the mobile header layout. I\'ve ensured the GK Services logo appears on the left, and the hamburger menu icon is positioned on the right. The plan is for the mobile header to *only* display the logo and hamburger menu, removing the `Connect Bay` and `Export ZIP` buttons, to simplify the mobile user experience. The buttons will reside inside the off-canvas drawer menu, and the desktop view will retain the full navigation and action buttons. I\'ve validated that no other buttons are present in the header.\n\n\n**Designing the Interactive Viewer**\n\nI\'m now putting together the design for the interactive viewer component. I\'m focusing on the Sketchfab integration using their Embed API, specifically targeting the sports car model. I\'ve got the necessary URL structure and I\'m developing the telemetry HUD overlay, planning to include features like fullscreen toggle, reset/reload options, and a hotspot diagnostic guide to highlight critical parts for inspection. I\'ll also add a direct link back to the model.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 824211910
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
