    thinking: "**Analyzing Visibility Constraints**\n\nOkay, so I was looking closely at `Header.tsx` and found a specific button component. It turns out the button\'s visibility was controlled by the `hidden md:inline-flex` class. This is the crucial part. I am understanding now how the display of the Contact button is being controlled based on screen size.\n\n\n**Adjusting Button Visibility**\n\nI realized that by changing the `hidden lg:inline-flex` class, both the \"Export ZIP\" and \"Connect Bay\" buttons will be hidden on mobile views (less than 1024px). Only the logo and hamburger toggle will be visible in the header. Further analysis shifted to the offcanvas drawer. It was clear that the header\'s sticky positioning and backdrop effects prevented full-screen overlap. Using `createPortal` should resolve this constraint.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile Menu**\n\nI\'ve been working on the off-canvas drawer\'s implementation for mobile. Using `createPortal` with `document.body` is working as expected to ensure it fully overlaps everything, including sticky headers and 3D content. I have added `useEffect` to the component to effectively lock the body scroll when the mobile menu is open. Now I\'m focusing on rewriting the nav link headings to reduce the menu\'s congestion.\n\n\n**Optimizing Navigation Links**\n\nI\'m now comparing the desktop menu titles: \"Overview,\" \"3D Inspection,\" and so on, with the navigation links. My focus is reducing clutter in the mobile menu. I am planning to reduce the mobile menu\'s congestion by making the titles more like the desktop version.\n\n\n"
