  planner_response {
    response: "I have addressed all three items:\n\n### 1. True Full-Screen Overlapping Offcanvas Navigation\n- **Portal Rendering**: Moved the offcanvas overlay and drawer directly to the root DOM (`document.body`) via React\'s `createPortal` with `fixed inset-0 z-[99999]`, ensuring it cleanly overlaps all viewport content, sticky headers, 3D canvases, and floating widgets.\n- **Scroll Locking**: Integrated an automated viewport scroll lock (`document.body.style.overflow = \'hidden\'`) while the offcanvas drawer is open, preventing page shift.\n- **Smooth Transition**: Added high-performance slide-left (`animate-slideLeft`) and backdrop fade (`animate-fadeIn`) keyframes with a darkened backdrop blur.\n\n### 2. Integrated 3D Sports Car Model (Sketchfab `dba4f043e0974054b5756d601ff5c256`)\n- **Direct 3D Model Integration**: Embedded the exact sports car model from your Sketchfab link (`dba4f043e0974054b5756d601ff5c256`) into an interactive WebGL 3D viewer (`SketchfabCarViewer`) as the primary default inspection engine.\n- **Full Orbital Freedom**: Visitors can orbit 360\302\260 around the sports car, zoom into aerodynamic splitters, pan with right-click, toggle full-screen mode, and trigger component telemetry diagnostics (Front Splitter, Ceramic Brakes, Carbon Aerodynamics, Exhaust Diffuser) directly on the vehicle.\n- **Engine Switcher**: Users can also toggle between this **Sports Car 3D**, the procedural **Three.js Hypercar**, and the **Multi-Elevation Studio**.\n\n### 3. De-congested Menu Headings & Clean Mobile Header\n- **Rewritten Navigation Headings**: Replaced the previous long titles and crowded badges with clean, scannable labels:\n  - **Overview** *(was \"Mission Hub\")*\n  - **3D Inspection** *(was \"360\302\260 Car Scan\" with pinging badge)*\n  - **Services** *(was \"Services Matrix\")*\n  - **Technology** *(was \"Robotic Bays\")*\n  - **Estimator** *(was \"Cost Terminal\")*\n  - **Reviews** *(was \"Reviews & FAQ\")*\n- **Mobile Header Button Hidden**: On all mobile and tablet viewports (`< 1024px`), the \"Connect Bay\" and \"Export ZIP\" buttons are hidden from the header bar, leaving strictly **only the GK Services Logo** on the left and the **Hamburger Menu Toggle** on the right. Both buttons remain accessible inside the overlapping offcanvas drawer."
    thinking: "**Verifying Initial Requests**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that the \'lint\\_applet\' and \'compile\\_applet\' processes are both passing. Now, I\'m verifying the initial user requests, specifically, that the off-canvas hamburger menu doesn\'t overlap. It seems rendering the off-canvas navigation has resolved this issue.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have addressed all three items:\n\n### 1. True Full-Screen Overlapping Offcanvas Navigation\n- **Portal Rendering**: Moved the offcanvas overlay and drawer directly to the root DOM (`document.body`) via React\'s `createPortal` with `fixed inset-0 z-[99999]`, ensuring it cleanly overlaps all viewport content, sticky headers, 3D canvases, and floating widgets.\n- **Scroll Locking**: Integrated an automated viewport scroll lock (`document.body.style.overflow = \'hidden\'`) while the offcanvas drawer is open, preventing page shift.\n- **Smooth Transition**: Added high-performance slide-left (`animate-slideLeft`) and backdrop fade (`animate-fadeIn`) keyframes with a darkened backdrop blur.\n\n### 2. Integrated 3D Sports Car Model (Sketchfab `dba4f043e0974054b5756d601ff5c256`)\n- **Direct 3D Model Integration**: Embedded the exact sports car model from your Sketchfab link (`dba4f043e0974054b5756d601ff5c256`) into an interactive WebGL 3D viewer (`SketchfabCarViewer`) as the primary default inspection engine.\n- **Full Orbital Freedom**: Visitors can orbit 360\302\260 around the sports car, zoom into aerodynamic splitters, pan with right-click, toggle full-screen mode, and trigger component telemetry diagnostics (Front Splitter, Ceramic Brakes, Carbon Aerodynamics, Exhaust Diffuser) directly on the vehicle.\n- **Engine Switcher**: Users can also toggle between this **Sports Car 3D**, the procedural **Three.js Hypercar**, and the **Multi-Elevation Studio**.\n\n### 3. De-congested Menu Headings & Clean Mobile Header\n- **Rewritten Navigation Headings**: Replaced the previous long titles and crowded badges with clean, scannable labels:\n  - **Overview** *(was \"Mission Hub\")*\n  - **3D Inspection** *(was \"360\302\260 Car Scan\" with pinging badge)*\n  - **Services** *(was \"Services Matrix\")*\n  - **Technology** *(was \"Robotic Bays\")*\n  - **Estimator** *(was \"Cost Terminal\")*\n  - **Reviews** *(was \"Reviews & FAQ\")*\n- **Mobile Header Button Hidden**: On all mobile and tablet viewports (`< 1024px`), the \"Connect Bay\" and \"Export ZIP\" buttons are hidden from the header bar, leaving strictly **only the GK Services Logo** on the left and the **Hamburger Menu Toggle** on the right. Both buttons remain accessible inside the overlapping offcanvas drawer."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 595807440
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
