  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Font Requirements**\n\nOkay, I\'m now drilling down into the font specifications. It seems we need distinct font treatments for light and dark versions. Light needs Lexend, and dark needs Kanit, specifically the 600 weight. The details are clear, so I\'m moving on to consider the implementation strategy.\n\n\n**Implementing Font Changes**\n\nI\'ve worked out the practical implementation of the font choices, and I think it\'s looking good. I have a clear plan to incorporate the Google Fonts links in `index.html`. In `index.css`, I have defined the `--font-primary`, `--font-secondary`, `--font-body` variables for both light and dark modes, specifying Lexend and Kanit 600 weight respectively. I am also working on typography utility classes for easy implementation.\n\n\n**Refining Logo Design**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the logo. The key is a futuristic, sharp design. My idea is an angular cyber-shield or hex monogram. The GK glyph will have speed slashes and a neon glow. The typography should be bold and futuristic. \"GK SERVICES\" is the core text, and the sub-text must go.\n\n\n**Designing Car Customization**\n\nI\'m now detailing the interactive 3D car customization. I\'m focusing on user control and creative expression. I have established distinct options for the user to change the 3D car body paint color and finish type. I have listed ten colors, including cyber cyan, and I have three types for the finish, including Gloss Metallic and Satin Matte. I am also working on creating four distinct rim options such as Aero-Turbine Disc, each with a color option. I am also working on two tire options, including racing slicks.\n\n\n**Expanding Car Customization**\n\nI\'m now integrating new car customization elements. I\'ve designed several tire options, including High-Grip Sport Grooves, Cyber Neon Glow Ring, and All-Weather Rain Tread. I am also working on brake caliper colors, like Electric Cyan and Brembo Track Red, and Aerodynamic Spoiler/Wing styles. I\'m also including neon underglow options and upgraded headlight and taillight styles. I also have several interactive engagements to work on for the user\'s enjoyment.\n\n\n**Adding Interactive Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating engaging interactions for the car customizer. I\'ve designed interactive buttons to spin the tires, simulating motion blur, and a \"Laser LiDAR Scan Mode\" with a holographic wireframe. There is also a \"Randomize Build\" option for a fun surprise and a \"Reset to Factory Spec\" to revert to the base model. Full 360\302\260 orbit and zoom, along with camera view presets, are also in progress. I\'m making sure that the new interactive 3D customizer is now the default viewer engine.\n\n\n**Refining 3D Model Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Sketchfab model. I am including multi-axis photography to complement the 3D model, to improve the user\'s experience.\n\n**Proofreading and Alignment**\n\nI\'m now meticulously proofreading the website content. In `mockCarData.ts`, I\'ve corrected \"Facia\" to \"Fascia\" and standardized to \"Monobloc.\" I\'ve also verified \"GK SERVICES\" is strictly used for the logo and footer. I\'ve updated the \"ContactModal.tsx\" to read \"Return to Overview\". I am also working on `Header.tsx` to properly align the header menu.\n\n\n**Centering the Header**\n\nI\'ve been working on getting the header centered correctly and have a solution. Because the logo and action buttons on each side have different widths, `justify-between` wasn\'t cutting it. I\'ve switched to a `relative flex` container, with the desktop navigation menu using absolute positioning. This approach guarantees that the navigation menu is strictly centered on the screen viewport and header.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 546179138
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
