  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding Theme Toggle**\n\nI\'ve been examining `Header.tsx` and realized the theme toggle was missing from lines 145-177! The component wasn\'t being rendered in the header, so it needed to be added. Now, I\'m working to include the theme toggle button for light/dark mode, focusing on the desktop view first.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme Toggle**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a clearer vision for the theme toggle\'s placement now. I\'m thinking of adding it to the header layout. For desktop, it should sit alongside \"Export ZIP\" and \"Connect Bay\". On mobile, let\'s nest it beside the hamburger toggle! I also want the toggle within the offcanvas drawer. I\'ve updated the component layout to reflect this.\n\n\n**Refining Navigation Links**\n\nI\'m focused on the navigation links now. I\'m examining the styling, particularly the active state and hover effects, to ensure a consistent look and feel across different screen sizes. I am particularly interested in adjusting the spacing and padding to enhance visual clarity and usability, making sure that it looks great, and is highly user-friendly. I\'m also ensuring the links are responsive and adapt to various viewport sizes.\n\n\n**Centering Menu Navigation**\n\nI\'ve just centered the navigation menu, and it\'s looking much better now. No matter what buttons are to the right, it is mathematically locked to the exact horizontal center of the header! Moreover, I am integrating the theme toggle directly, allowing the user to switch between \"Dark (Kanit 600)\" and \"Light (Lexend)\" modes instantly. The logo is now a strictly defined link.\n\n\n**Refining Cyber Monogram**\n\nI\'m now diving into the cyber-monogram. I\'m focusing on refining its visual details, specifically the hover effects and transitions. My goal is to ensure it has a futuristic and appealing appearance, with smooth transitions and a clear visual hierarchy. I am also working on the gradient overlay, and ensuring the monogram scales properly.\n\n\n**Designing Car Customizer**\n\nI\'m now completely focused on designing the car customizer. I\'m imagining a 3D workshop and am exploring `Car3DCanvas.tsx` for possible component breakdowns. I\'m thinking about providing states for `bodyColor` (with a hex string, finish types), `rimStyle` (various styles, sizes), and `tireType` (radial, low-profile). I\'m looking at implementing a customizable 3D model with interactive controls for a truly engaging experience.\n\n\n**Defining Wheel Styles**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the car customizer, focusing on wheels! I\'m adding `aero`, `cyber-mesh`, and `concave-star` rim styles. I\'m also including silver, gold, black, and cyan options for rim color. Then, I\'m working to include tire options!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 330997412
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
