  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the requested updates and refinements across the site:\n\n- **3D Vehicle Customizer & Playground**:\n  - **Body Paint & Finishes**: Added real-time body paint color switching across 9 racing and cyber hues, toggleable between **Metallic**, **Matte**, and **Pearl** clearcoat finishes.\n  - **Forged Rims & Calipers**: Integrated 4 rim architectures (**Forged 5-Spoke**, **Aero-Turbine Disc**, **Cyber Dual-Mesh**, and **Deep Concave Star**) with customizable rim finishes and ceramic brake caliper colors.\n  - **Tire Compounds**: Enabled selection of **Track Racing Slicks** (with sidewall decals), **Sport Directional Grooves**, **Cyber Neon Glow Rings**, and **All-Weather Ribs**.\n  - **Aerodynamics & Underglow**: Provided real-time spoiler customization (**GT Carbon Wing**, **Carbon Ducktail Lip**, **Active Twin Airbrakes**, and **Flush Streamline**), along with pulsating neon ground underglow and high-beam laser headlight controls.\n  - **Engine Rev & Wheel Spin**: Added an interactive rev trigger that revs the engine, flashes exhaust flames, and spins the custom wheels with synthesized audio feedback.\n\n- **Header Alignment & Responsive Refinement**:\n  - **Centered Menu**: Centered the desktop navigation with clean, non-congested headings.\n  - **Mobile Header**: Streamlined the mobile view to display strictly the futuristic **GK SERVICES** logo and the hamburger menu, moving secondary actions and the theme toggle into the slide-out offcanvas drawer.\n\n- **Site-Wide Proofreading**:\n  - Audited all section files, mock data, and modal dialogs to correct technical and automotive terminology (e.g., standardizing \"Fascia\", \"Tire\", and diagnostic tolerances)."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Requirements Fulfilled**\n\nI\'ve successfully built the project and now I\'m carefully examining the user\'s requirements from Checkpoint 3, especially the outstanding items. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the font style requests for both light and dark versions, making sure the Lexend and Kanit fonts are properly applied. I want to confirm that all required font styling changes are implemented before I proceed further.\n\n\n**Verifying Font Application**\n\nI\'ve verified that `index.html` correctly loads the required Lexend and Kanit fonts, including the italic and weight variations. I\'ve also confirmed that `src/index.css` correctly sets the font-family and weight based on the user\'s requirements.\n\nI\'ve checked that the futuristic logo replaces the original and only \"GK SERVICES\" is present. Furthermore, I\'ve successfully implemented a 3D car customizer, enabling users to modify paint, rims, tires, brake calipers, and spoilers. The implementation includes numerous options for a realistic and interactive experience.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the requested updates and refinements across the site:\n\n- **3D Vehicle Customizer & Playground**:\n  - **Body Paint & Finishes**: Added real-time body paint color switching across 9 racing and cyber hues, toggleable between **Metallic**, **Matte**, and **Pearl** clearcoat finishes.\n  - **Forged Rims & Calipers**: Integrated 4 rim architectures (**Forged 5-Spoke**, **Aero-Turbine Disc**, **Cyber Dual-Mesh**, and **Deep Concave Star**) with customizable rim finishes and ceramic brake caliper colors.\n  - **Tire Compounds**: Enabled selection of **Track Racing Slicks** (with sidewall decals), **Sport Directional Grooves**, **Cyber Neon Glow Rings**, and **All-Weather Ribs**.\n  - **Aerodynamics & Underglow**: Provided real-time spoiler customization (**GT Carbon Wing**, **Carbon Ducktail Lip**, **Active Twin Airbrakes**, and **Flush Streamline**), along with pulsating neon ground underglow and high-beam laser headlight controls.\n  - **Engine Rev & Wheel Spin**: Added an interactive rev trigger that revs the engine, flashes exhaust flames, and spins the custom wheels with synthesized audio feedback.\n\n- **Header Alignment & Responsive Refinement**:\n  - **Centered Menu**: Centered the desktop navigation with clean, non-congested headings.\n  - **Mobile Header**: Streamlined the mobile view to display strictly the futuristic **GK SERVICES** logo and the hamburger menu, moving secondary actions and the theme toggle into the slide-out offcanvas drawer.\n\n- **Site-Wide Proofreading**:\n  - Audited all section files, mock data, and modal dialogs to correct technical and automotive terminology (e.g., standardizing \"Fascia\", \"Tire\", and diagnostic tolerances)."
