  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Fetch Compatibility**\n\nI\'ve been examining the behavior of `fetch` across different environments. Notably, `undici` in Node.js lacks `file://` support, which is a key difference. However, Vite seamlessly handles HTTP GET requests for both WebAssembly and GLB files in both development and production builds, making the deployment of files easy. I\'m focusing on these inconsistencies to understand the nuances of the environments.\n\n\n**Considering Draco Integration**\n\nI\'m now exploring `DRACOLoader` for model optimization. I\'ve been experimenting with `setDecoderPath` and `setDecoderConfig` to manage decoding and fallbacks. I\'m focusing on incorporating this into the model loading process within `Car3DCanvas.tsx`, specifically considering graceful error handling for decoding issues. I\'m currently assessing options like WASM for Draco decoding and determining how to handle potential performance bottlenecks.\n\n\n**Refining Model Scaling & Materials**\n\nI\'m now focusing on model scaling within the loading process, adjusting scale based on dimensions to ensure a consistent size. I\'m also refining material and mesh collection via traversal, specifically tagging meshes for body, rims, brakes, tires, glass, and carbon fiber. This includes considerations of color customization for the body and the implications on material identification. My goal is to streamline the subsequent material assignment and interactive customizations.\n\n\n**Exploring Color and Finishes**\n\nI\'m now diving into the customization options. I\'m focusing on implementing a custom hex color picker and various finish modes, including Gloss Clearcoat, Satin Matte, Metallic Flake, and Liquid Chameleon. I\'m considering real-time clearcoat, roughness, and metalness sliders for greater control. I\'m also planning options for wheels, rims, brake calipers, and aerodynamic spoilers, along with interactive window tint levels.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 892354246
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
