    thinking: "**Analyzing Procedural Body**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `Car3DCanvas.tsx` file, specifically line 414. I\'ve noted the creation of a procedural car body group, designed to act as a fallback while the GLTF model loads. This seems to involve a `THREE.Group` being added to the main `carGroup`, and the use of `proceduralBodyRef`. This procedural approach is intriguing, I wonder how it\'s implemented.\n\n\n**Exploring Model Loading**\n\nNow, I\'m delving deeper into the GLB model loading, specifically within the `gltfLoader.load` callback. It appears the authentic sports car model is loaded from `/models/sports-car.glb`. The code then centers and aligns the model on the stage floor. I\'m noting the use of `DRACOLoader` for optimization. It looks like the model\'s bounding box is calculated to center it on the grid. This is key.\n\n\n**Refining Material Application**\n\nI\'m now examining how materials are being applied to the loaded 3D model. I\'ve noted the `model.traverse` method is key, and it appears the code iterates through all meshes, applying specific materials based on mesh names or existing material names. I\'ve noticed special handling for the body, glass, carbon fiber, rims, and brakes, and the materials are all being handled with physical material properties. I am specifically investigating how paint, glass and carbon fiber are rendered.\n\n\n\n"
