  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed all the requested enhancements to the application:\n\n- **Hero Section Visual Elevation**:\n  - **Live Workshop Chamber Preview**: Added an operational service bay strip featuring high-resolution photography of active supercars (Ferrari 488 Pista in ceramic curing, Porsche 911 GT3 undergoing camber alignment, and McLaren 720S on the dyno).\n  - **Photographic Pillar Cards**: Replaced the plain metric boxes with rich image-header cards for **LiDAR 48-Pt Scan**, **9H Graphene Shield**, and **Synchronized Dyno**, complete with contrast overlays and laser-tolerance tags.\n  - **Section Differentiation**: Structured clear visual boundaries between the Hero Section and the studio workspaces using technical badge dividers and balanced tonal contrast.\n\n- **Tab Reordering**:\n  - Reordered the 3D inspection studio tabs to the requested sequence:\n    1. **Sports Car 3D** (High-poly 3D interactive viewer)\n    2. **Multi-Elevation Studio** (360\302\260 multi-elevation orbital inspection with vehicle gallery)\n    3. **3D Car Customizer** (Three.js customizer with paint finishes, wheels, and aero tuning)\n\n- **Multi-Elevation Studio Car Gallery**:\n  - Integrated the vehicle fleet selector into the Multi-Elevation Studio, allowing quick switching between hypercars (Ferrari 488 Pista, Porsche 911 GT3 RS, McLaren 720S Spider, Lamborghini Hurac\303\241n Tecnica, and Aston Martin Vantage GT).\n  - Added category filters (*All Fleet*, *Track Special*, *Aero Coupe*, *Super Sports*) and live vehicle telemetry footers displaying 0\342\200\223100 times, downforce, and chassis scores.\n\n- **Authentic 3D Sports Car Model in Customizer**:\n  - Integrated the authentic 3D sports car model via Three.js with Draco compression decoding.\n  - Connected the real car body, glass canopy, carbon fiber diffusers, and alloy wheels to the customization controls:\n    - Real-time paint finish adjustment (Metallic, Matte, Pearl)\n    - Rim and brake caliper color updates\n    - Active downforce wings (GT Wing, Ducktail Lip, Active Twin Vanes)\n    - Engine revving with real-time wheel spinning and exhaust glow lights\n    - Sub-millimeter LiDAR hotspot targets mapped across the chassis\n\n- **Global Color Palette Update**:\n  - **Dark Mode**: Primary `#171719`, Secondary `#D75151` (Rosso Crimson)\n  - **Light Mode**: Primary `#252642`, Secondary `#8A6A4A` (Bronze Titanium)\n  - Colors are integrated across the design system, CSS variables, hover states, and paint finish selectors."
    thinking: "**Reviewing User Requirements**\n\nI\'ve got good news! The applet compiled successfully. Now, I\'m meticulously checking the user\'s checklist to ensure everything is perfect. Specifically, I\'ve added images to the hero section, including a Ferrari service preview strip, to make it visually appealing. I\'m focusing on ensuring all requirements are comprehensively met.\n\n\n**Updating Visuals and Layout**\n\nI\'ve just added real photography thumbnails for the 488, 911 GT3, and 720S. I\'ve enhanced the Hero Pillar cards with high-definition imagery and telemetry indicators. Additionally, I\'ve adjusted visual differentiation between sections using badges and background contrast. Furthermore, I\'ve moved the 3D Car Customizer to the last tab and adjusted the tab layout, while integrating a new studio car gallery. This now features a fleet selector and category filtering.\n\n\n"
